From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Fursund <jens@spectralcompute.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Duplicate search channels below sm90 as on Ampere

ncclTopoDupChannels skips the duplication when ccMin > 80, bwIntra < 50
and there are more than 4 channels. Below sm90 the search speeds are
Ampere's (at most 40 GB/s intra-node, 48 inter-node), so for sm86 and
sm89 bwIntra < 50 always holds, and the condition is only "more than 4
channels": the same topology gets half the channels of an A100. Hopper
and newer search at up to 60 GB/s, so for them the condition also
depends on bandwidth.

Example: a full mesh of 4 GPUs with 4 NVLinks (80 GB/s) per pair, as on
a 4-GPU HGX A100. The search finds 6 ring orders at 40 GB/s. With cc 8.0
they are duplicated to 12 at 20 GB/s and ncclTopoPostset makes 24
channels. With cc 8.9 the duplication is skipped and NCCL runs 12
channels, about 4 per link.

This lifts the 4-channel limit for sm86 and sm89 only; sm80 and sm90
and newer are unchanged. On NVIDIA GPUs it changes a topology only if
the search finds more than 4 channels at 25 GB/s or more.

4x MI300A through SCALE (which reports cc 8.9; xGMI full mesh, 4 links
of 20 GB/s per pair in NVML), with the PCI class 0x1200 fix, nccl-tests
-g 4, 256 MiB, bus bandwidth, 12 -> 24 channels: all_reduce 151 -> 210
GB/s, all_gather 147 -> 201, reduce_scatter 127 -> 170, broadcast 162
-> 227, reduce 140 -> 200. More channels than 24 (NCCL_MIN_NCHANNELS 32,
48, 64) add nothing.
---
diff --git a/src/graph/search.cc b/src/graph/search.cc
index cbae02f..361d53d 100644
--- a/src/graph/search.cc
+++ b/src/graph/search.cc
@@ -963,7 +963,7 @@ ncclResult_t ncclTopoDupChannels(struct ncclTopoGraph* graph, int ccMin, int ngp
   if (graph->nChannels == 0) return ncclSuccess;
   if (graph->pattern == NCCL_TOPO_PATTERN_NVLS) return ncclSuccess;
   if (graph->bwIntra < 25.0) return ncclSuccess;
-  if (ccMin > 80 && graph->bwIntra < 50.0 && graph->nChannels > 4) return ncclSuccess;
+  if (ccMin >= 90 && graph->bwIntra < 50.0 && graph->nChannels > 4) return ncclSuccess;
 
   int dupChannels = std::min(graph->nChannels*2, graph->maxChannels);
   memcpy(graph->intra+graph->nChannels*ngpus, graph->intra, (dupChannels-graph->nChannels)*ngpus*sizeof(int));
